From 840a939ee526137639665ff5f587224d6a36403f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Nelson <mcnster@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:03:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32/tests: Test signature verification with unsorted
 authenticated attributes.

The test message is a PKCS#7 SignedData whose authenticated attributes
are deliberately not in ascending DER SET OF order, with the signature
computed over that order.  OpenSSL verifies it successfully.

It was generated with a throwaway 2048-bit RSA key by reversing the
attribute set of an ordinary signed message and re-signing over the
result, so it contains no third-party data.  The test fails without the
preceding change.

Signed-off-by: Michael Nelson <mcnster@gmail.com>
---
 dlls/crypt32/tests/msg.c | 166 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 166 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/tests/msg.c b/dlls/crypt32/tests/msg.c
index e2d9a15145b5..6b987f84b023 100644
--- a/dlls/crypt32/tests/msg.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/tests/msg.c
@@ -3887,6 +3887,171 @@ static void test_verify_ecc_signature(void)
     CryptMsgClose(msg);
 }
 
